  "content": {
    "title": "Noah Kahan’s Netflix doc airs in less than a week. Why he's nervous",
    "text": "April 9, 2026, 4:21 p.m. ETNew Englanders are counting down the days until the next album from Watertown, Massachusetts, resident Noah Kahan. However, before Kahan releases his album, he is releasing a movie.On Monday, March 16, the Vermont-born musician announced on Instagram that a new Netflix documentary titled \"Noah Kahan: Out of Body\" will officially drop on April 13. The release date is just 11 days before the release of Kahan's fourth studio album, \"The Great Divide.\"Here's what to know about Noah Kahan's new documentary, as well as how to watch it.What is Noah Kahan's documentary about?According to a press release from Netflix, \"Noah Kahan: Out of Body\" follows Kahan after the success of \"Stick Season\" as he returns home to Vermont. \"Buoyed by his uncanny wit, he searches for a sense of home and creative inspiration as he confronts the deeply personal struggles that have left him out of sync with himself,\" reads the release.Kahan shared in his Instagram post that the documentary gives an extremely personal look at the musician's life, featuring painful topics and moments with his family.\"My life was filmed for a year and a half. It was weird, difficult, and genuinely beautiful to experience,\" Kahan wrote in his caption. \"This documentary captures so much more than I ever thought the world would see about myself, my creative journey and my family. I am nervous about it because it's personal and some things I touch on are painful to think about and be reminded of. I remember though that anything scary or hard is usually worth sharing with the world.\"How to watch Noah Kahan's documentaryAs of Monday, April 13, \"Noah Kahan: Out of Body\" will be available to watch exclusively on Netflix.",
